This dossier supports first-time, never-licensed applicants preparing for the regular passenger-car written knowledge and road sign tests in Michigan. The issuing authority is the Michigan Department of State, led by the Secretary of State, and the source is the handbook What Every Driver Must Know. This section covers commercial vehicles with their stopping distances, no zones and wide turns, passing trucks safely, slow-moving vehicles and horse-drawn buggies, pedestrians including those with white canes or guide dogs, children, motorcycles, scooters and mopeds, bicyclists with the passing distance law, and autocycles. The handbook pages do not state an official question count, passing score, test format or time limit for the Secretary of State knowledge test, so this dossier asserts no value for any of them and records each as an explicit unknown. Practice scoring follows only the accepted LearningLoop product policy, never an official threshold.
